-- title:
--   Rational place from a non-maximal prime with transcendental j
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a commutative local ring, $\kappa$ an algebraically closed field, and $\theta$ a bijective ring homomorphism from the residue field of $A_0$ to $\kappa$. Let $C$ be an $A_0$-algebra which is a domain, $j\in C$ an element such that $C$ is module-finite over the $A_0$-subalgebra generated by $j$, let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$, and let $\psi : C \to \mathrm{ResidueField}(A_0)$ be an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism with $\psi(c)=0$ exactly for $c\in y$. Let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime ideal of $C$ with $\mathfrak p \le y$ and $\mathfrak p \ne y$, such that the image in $C$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ lies in $\mathfrak p$, and such that for every polynomial $f$ over $A_0$ with $f(j)\in\mathfrak p$ all coefficients of $f$ lie in the maximal ideal of $A_0$. Then there exist a field $\Omega$, a $\kappa$-algebra structure on it, a place $V$ of $\Omega$ over $\kappa$ — that is, a valuation subring of $\Omega$ containing the image of $\kappa$, different from $\Omega$, and all of whose ideals are principal — a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}$ from the residue field of $V$ to $\kappa$, and a ring homomorphism $\rho : C \to V$, such that: $\mathrm{res}$ restricted along $\kappa \to \mathrm{ResidueField}(V)$ is the identity of $\kappa$; for every $a\in A_0$ the image of $\rho(a)$ in $\Omega$ is the image of $\theta(\mathrm{res}_{A_0}(a))$ under $\kappa\to\Omega$; $\mathrm{res}$ of the residue class of $\rho(c)$ equals $\theta(\psi(c))$ for all $c\in C$; the image of $\rho(j)$ in $\Omega$ is transcendental over $\kappa$; $\Omega$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\kappa(\rho(j))$; and for $c\in C$ the image of $\rho(c)$ in $\Omega$ vanishes exactly when $c\in\mathfrak p$.
--
--   This packages the passage from a non-maximal prime $\mathfrak p$ of $C$, residually transcendental in $j$, to a $\kappa$-rational place of the one-variable function field $\Omega$ obtained from $C/\mathfrak p$, together with a reading map $\rho$ whose kernel clause transports congruences modulo $\mathfrak p$ into $\Omega$; the valuation ring is produced by Chevalley's extension theorem and is $\kappa$-rational because $\kappa$ is algebraically closed. It is used in the analysis of Tate points and of chart algebras on modular curves of full level.
-- source:
